      "fullsize": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:hovt6k22s64dq63jjmoyibk3/bafkreigolbpzr6cnoz3gcr25da62fkutil2tmsumximklpgoql3dvsdxdi",
      "alt": "The Shoggoth who came to read",
      "ratio": 1.2278,
      "handle": "dave.9000ish.uk",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/dave.9000ish.uk/post/3mwyjxd5gyc2v",
      "uri": "at://did:plc:hovt6k22s64dq63jjmoyibk3/app.bsky.feed.post/3mwyjxd5gyc2v",
      "likeCount": 12
    },
    {
      "thumb": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_thumbnail/plain/did:plc:hovt6k22s64dq63jjmoyibk3/bafkreih35i6wy76umnldmftl7bux67jojrn66umqiiv34x4hcpilgq2cci",
      "fullsize": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:hovt6k22s64dq63jjmoyibk3/bafkreih35i6wy76umnldmftl7bux67jojrn66umqiiv34x4hcpilgq2cci",
      "alt": "Once there was a little girl called Thea, and she was having tea with her mummy in the kitchen.\nSuddenly there was a ring at the door.\nThea’s mummy said, “I wonder who that can be. It can’t be the milkman because he came this morning. And it can’t be boy from the grocer because this isn’t the day he comes.\nAnd it can’t be Daddy because he’s got his key. We’d better open the door and see.”\n\nThea opened the door, and there was a big, tentacled, many-eyed shoggoth. The shoggoth said, “Excuse me, but I’m very hungry for knowledge. Do you have any books?”\nThea’s mummy said, “Of course, come in.”\nSo the shoggoth came into the study and sat down at the desk.",
      "ratio": 1.2278,
      "handle": "dave.9000ish.uk",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/dave.9000ish.uk/post/3mwyjxd5gyc2v",
      "uri": "at://did:plc:hovt6k22s64dq63jjmoyibk3/app.bsky.feed.post/3mwyjxd5gyc2v",
      "likeCount": 12
    },
    {
      "thumb": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_thumbnail/plain/did:plc:hovt6k22s64dq63jjmoyibk3/bafkreieqwc2roc6ip4fflt6qlangujlxa4mweyhksxdf6u6el54uui36lm",
      "fullsize": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:hovt6k22s64dq63jjmoyibk3/bafkreieqwc2roc6ip4fflt6qlangujlxa4mweyhksxdf6u6el54uui36lm",
      "alt": "Thea’s mummy said, “Would you like a novel?” But the shoggoth didn’t just take one novel. He took all the novels off the shelves and his many tentacles held them up to his many eyes.\n\nWhirp!\n\nHe read them so fast the pages flew apart.\n\nAnd he still looked hungry, so Thea passed him volume 1 of the encyclopedia britannica.\n\nBut again the shoggoth didn’t read just one volume. He read all 32 volumes. And then he read all the newspapers and all the magazines, and all the non-fiction until there was nothing left in the study but whisps of paper.",
