    {
      "thumb": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_thumbnail/plain/did:plc:gjqw6pjl2wvndjlmatxpenkz/bafkreidlhtzfkblfu6vgidamdvftryxpai4l64xoveoy5vezpc6uox2chq",
      "fullsize": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:gjqw6pjl2wvndjlmatxpenkz/bafkreidlhtzfkblfu6vgidamdvftryxpai4l64xoveoy5vezpc6uox2chq",
      "alt": "No desktop GIS like QGIS or ArcGIS. It's all code, and OpenStreetMap is one of several data sources:\n\n  - Renderer: MapLibre GL JS 6 (open-source WebGL maps) running inside Remotion. It draws the 3D globe, terrain,\n    hillshade and elevation colour ramp live for every frame.\n  - Data:\n    - River lines: OpenStreetMap, pulled by Wikidata ID through the Overpass API.\n    - River identification: Wikidata, which turns fweet's names into specific rivers.\n    - Elevation: AWS Terrain Tiles (Mapzen terrarium DEM).\n    - Satellite imagery: Esri World Imagery.\n    - The faint blue background waterways: OpenFreeMap vector tiles (OpenStreetMap data).\n  - Processing: Python with shapely to merge, simplify and stitch the Liffey's pieces into one line, plus my own camera,\n    timing and portal planning in plan.py.\n  - Tiles: a small caching tile server of my own (tools/tileproxy.py), so renders are fast and come out the same every\n    time.",
